# Walkthrough - WorldLoop Test Suite Stabilization

I have stabilized the WorldLoop test suite by fixing 8 failing unit tests and implementing Docker port isolation to prevent conflicts with production environments.

## Changes Made

### 1. Unit Test Fixes
- **TypeError Mitigation**: Fixed comparisons between `MagicMock` and numbers in [AIBrain](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/src/ai/brain.py#37-199) and [CombatAspect](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/src/core/aspects/combat.py#7-128) tests by providing explicit return values for [hp_ratio](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/src/core/models.py#108-113) and `age_ticks`.
- **AttributeError Resolution**: Corrected [FactionRegistry](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/src/core/faction.py#52-233) mocking to ensure [is_hostile](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/src/core/faction.py#93-95) is treated as a mockable method.
- **Quest System Scoping**: Fixed an `UnboundLocalError` in [generate_quest](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/src/core/quests.py#227-360) by ensuring `target_pos` is properly initialized at the start of the function.

### 2. Docker Port Isolation
- **[docker-compose.yml](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/docker-compose.yml)**: Parameterized all host ports using environment variables with sensible defaults.
- **[tests/e2e/conftest.py](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/tests/e2e/conftest.py)**: Added a dynamic port discovery mechanism that assigns free ports for each E2E test session.
- **[tests/e2e/test_production_stack.py](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/tests/e2e/test_production_stack.py)**: Updated tests to dynamically resolve URLs based on the assigned ports.

