## Remaining Skips
The 51 skipped tests are all located in [tests/e2e/test_production_stack.py](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/tests/e2e/test_production_stack.py). They were skipped with the following reason:
> `Skipped: Docker Compose not available, skipping E2E stack tests.`

This confirms that the skips are environmental. I have implemented **Docker Port Isolation** in [docker-compose.yml](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/docker-compose.yml) and [tests/e2e/conftest.py](file:///d:/Projects/rpg-based-simulation/tests/e2e/conftest.py) to ensure that when these tests are run in an environment with Docker, they will dynamically assign ports to avoid conflicts with your production setup.
